{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789393839,"nonce":"XZZFcJtIbBr74Sy8WVaRDzXq7yY=","title":"The interpreter's JIT cannot link the effect runtime on Linux and Windows","message":"`ZyntaxRuntime::register_function` and `register_function_typed` put a\nsymbol on the Cranelift backend but not in the interpreter's table, so\nthe JIT the interpreter installs (`install_interp_jit_with`) was never\nhanded `__zyntax_effect_lookup_op` and the other effect and box\nsymbols. It fell back to `dlsym`, which finds them in a macOS\nexecutable and in nothing linked without `-rdynamic`: CI's Linux and\nWindows lanes failed `an_imported_effect_can_be_performed` with\n\"can't resolve symbol __zyntax_effect_lookup_op\" while the same test\npassed on the Mac.\n\nBoth registration paths now mirror the symbol into the interpreter as\n`with_symbols` already did for the box runtime.","files":null}]}